 LQqwW3cL4sFhgbc3BagB6aoh10Q1WK8aQA/viewform)Water and AI. What AI Can Lear
 n from Water: October 1\, 6:30–8pm\, Worth Ryder Art GalleryTour of AI: 
 October 3 Register hereClosing day: October 3\, 12-3pm\, Worth Ryder Art G
 allery Open to the public\, no RSVP required Additional events\, details\,
  and registration links to be announced. Times subject to change\, please 
 also check the campus calendar (https://events.berkeley.edu/art). This exh
 ibition is supported by the France-Berkeley Fund of the Institute of Europ
 ean Studies\, the Department of German and the Department of Art Practice\
 , together with the Berkeley Center for New Media\, the Berkeley Institute
  for Data Science (BIDS)\, Department of Rhetoric\; Antikythera\, the Huma
 n Technology Futures (HTF)\, the Pamela P. Fong and Family Distinguished C
 hair in China Studies\, the Division of Arts & Humanities\, the Townsend C
 enter for the Humanities\, the School of Information\, the Technology Netw
 ork of the Berkeley Economy and Society Initiative (BESI)\, and the Berkel
 ey Art\, Law\, and Finance Project\, hosted by the Berkeley Center for Law
