SUMMARY:Exhibition: "Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and Hallucinations"
LOCATION:Worth Ryder Art Gallery\, Anthropology &amp\; Art Building\, Rm 1
 16
DESCRIPTION:The Department of German and the Department of Art Practice ar
 e excited to announce the opening of Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and
  Hallucinations\, curated by Antonio Somaini with Hannes Bajohr\, Sonja Th
 iel and Elena Yu\, in dialogue with the France–Berkeley research initiat
 ive The Latent Spaces of Culture\, and on display at the Worth Ryder Art G
 allery. In neural networks\, the "hidden layers" are the intermediate stra
 ta of transformation between input and output — the computational struct
 ures where data are transformed\, weighted\, and recombined into increasin
 gly abstract\, distributed representations that no human eye can read. The
  exhibition Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and Hallucinations takes thi
 s term as its conceptual frame\, bringing together seventeen international
  artists and researchers working at the intersection of contemporary art a
 nd machine learning to make visible what artificial intelligence keeps out
  of sight: its planetary infrastructures and computational latent spaces\,
  its colonial and ideological underpinnings\, its misrecognitions and hall
 ucinations\, and its transformation of our relation to the past through th
 e silent reprocessing of pre-existing cultural forms. The exhibition is or
 ganized in four sections: "In the Latent Spaces of Culture\," "Material In
 frastructures\," "Colonial Imaginaries: From Misrecognition to Generative 
 Slopaganda\," and "Hallucinations and Psychedelia." Featuring works by Nou
 f Aljowaysir (https://www.noufaljowaysir.com/)\; Gašper and Nina Beguš &
  Metahaven (https://latentspacecraft.antikythera.org/)\; Grégory Chatonsk
 y (https://chatonsky.net/)\; Kate Crawford & Vladan Joler (https://anatomy
 of.ai/)\; Asma Kazmi (https://www.asmakazmi.com/) & Jill Miller (https://w
 ww.jillmiller.net/)\; Andrea Kh��ra (https://www.andreakhora.com/)\; O
 ccitane Lacurie & Barnabé Sauvage (https://www.schirn.de/en/schirnmag/3-q
 uestions-for-occitane-lacurie-und-barnabe-sauvage/)\; Greg Niemeyer (https
 ://www.gregniemeyer.com/)\; and Mario Santamaria (https://mariosantamaria.
 net/) & Alex Saum-Pascual (https://www.alexsaum.com/).Hidden Layers is a c
 ollaboration between the Department of German and the Worth Ryder Art Gall
 ery at the Department of Art Practice. It is part of the France–Berkeley
  research initiative The Latent Spaces of Culture: a collaboration between
  UC Berkeley\, the Université Sorbonne Nouvelle in Paris\, and the French
  National Center for Scientific Research (CNRS).Exhibition Dates: Septembe
